  "answer_text": "Best practice is to put guest Wi‑Fi on a VLAN that lives on the Socket rather than a routed range behind an L3 switch. The Socket can act as the gateway and DHCP for each VLAN, and you can isolate a VLAN quickly with a WAN firewall rule or by removing its default gateway from CMA. For guests, configure an Internet‑only VLAN/range so they can reach only the Internet and not internal resources. Example: create a VLAN-enabled range named “Guest WIFI” with VLAN 100, subnet 10.1.0.0/24 and gateway 10.1.0.1 on the Socket (this is supported and can be managed from CMA).",
